(version 1)

# OpenDrone canonical design rules.
#
# Copied from hardware-template into every board repo. Keep the block above the
# marker byte-identical across repos. Board-specific rules go
# below the marker, never in the middle.
#
# This file holds CUSTOM rules only. The fab numbers that gate a JLCPCB order
# live in the project file under board.design_settings.rules, and come from
# Board Setup > Import Settings from Another Board, pointed at
# kicad/templates/OpenDrone-6L. The line standard is:
#
#   clearance 0.09   track 0.09   via 0.35 / 0.20 drill
#   annular 0.075    hole-to-hole 0.20        edge clearance 0.20
#
# Do not restate those here. Two copies of a number drift, and the one you are
# not looking at is the one that is wrong.

(rule "silkscreen over pad"
  (constraint silk_clearance (min 0.15mm))
  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad'"))

# --- board-specific rules below this line ------------------------------------
#
# Only what this board needs and the line does not. Name every rule so the next
# person can tell a real constraint from a copied one.
#
# 2 oz outer copper, same as the ESC boards: four power stages on 25.5 mm.
# Heavier copper etches with a wider taper, so the outer layers need 0.16 mm
# where the line standard is 0.09 mm. Inner layers stay at 1 oz and keep the
# standard. This is a rule and not a global minimum on purpose: raising the
# board minimum would constrain the signal routing on the inner layers for no
# reason. Anything narrower than 0.16 mm (USB pair, Analog, Default 0.09)
# therefore routes on the inner layers or gets widened where it surfaces.
#
# Only the Base is 2 oz. The Core (daughter board, same master PCB) is 1 oz
# outer and keeps the line standard. The rules therefore apply only inside the
# rule area named "Base" that covers the Base island in the master. It is
# written this way round on purpose: the interactive router does not evaluate
# area conditions reliably for the track it is drawing, and a rule that is
# missed while routing is caught by DRC, whereas a rule that is wrongly applied
# blocks routing the Core at 1 oz widths. The derived Base board carries the
# area, the derived Core board does not, so both check with the right rules
# from this one file.

(rule "2 oz outer copper, clearance"
  (constraint clearance (min 0.16mm))
  (layer outer)
  (condition "A.intersectsArea('Base') || B.intersectsArea('Base')"))

(rule "2 oz outer copper, track width"
  (constraint track_width (min 0.16mm))
  (layer outer)
  (condition "A.intersectsArea('Base')"))
